A framebuffer ebook viewer.

Build dependencies (detected via pkg-config):
- poppler-cpp (PDF rendering)
- libfyaml    (ereader.yml parsing)
- freetype2   (file manager text)

Run `make` to build. The file manager and the text reader draw UTF-8 text
(Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Cyrillic, Arabic, Thai, Devanagari, Hebrew, ...)
with the built-in font list: fonts are loaded in order and the later ones act
as fallbacks for characters the first font lacks. Set EREADER_FONT to an
absolute font file path to use it as the primary font. The file manager uses
12 px text and the text reader uses 10 px text (`FBM_FONT_SCALE` scales both
for the target screen).

File manager keys:
- e  enter the selected folder, open the selected PDF, or read a text file
- q  go to the parent folder
- j  select the next entry
- k  select the previous entry

Text reader keys:
- j  scroll down half a screen
- k  scroll up half a screen
- q  close the text reader

Like the PDF view, the file manager shows the status bar (page buttons,
battery, WiFi) along the bottom edge of the framebuffer.
